.TH CHMAP_CREATE_MP 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chmap_create_mp \- create a hash map with custom memory management procedures
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

chmap chmap_create_mp(size_t initial_bucket_array_size,
                      ccol_data_type key_type, ccol_data_type val_type,
                      ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mmgmt_procs, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a hash map that allocates through the given memory management
procedures. It is a thin inline wrapper over chmap_create_full(3) that
passes NULL for the custom hashing procedure, so the map uses its own
hashing for the key type.

The map picks its implementation strategy from the key and value types, as
chmap_create_full(3) describes, and an allocator does not change that
choice. Every allocation that the map makes later goes through these
procedures, including the allocations that an iterator over the map
makes, so the caller must destroy the map while these procedures are
still valid.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
initial_bucket_array_size  Initial capacity hint
key_type                   Key type, as a ccol_data_type
val_type                   Value type, as a ccol_data_type
mmgmt_procs                Memory management procedures, or NULL for the
                           default allocator
err                        Optional pointer that receives an error string on
                           failure, or NULL
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A newly created map on success.
NULL on failure, with *err set to an error string when err is non-NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Failure is reported rather than fatal; the chmap_construct_mp(3) macro
layer calls ccol_fatal_err() instead
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_create (3),
.BR chmap_create_full (3),
.BR chmap_construct_mp (3),
.BR chmap_init_mp (3),
.BR chmap_destroy (3)
